.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
docs
tests
data
models
# Docker's ignore patterns do NOT recurse: the bare `.venv` above matches only
# the one at the context root. A cold `kind-up-full.sh` was shipping 400MB+ of
# build context because frontend/node_modules and the virtualenvs inside
# .claude/worktrees (one holds a full CPU torch install) were all being sent.
# None of it is used by any Dockerfile - the images install their own deps.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.claude
.github
*.md

# Same non-recursive trap as `.venv` above: the bare `tests` and `docs` entries
# match ONLY the ones at the context root, so every per-service suite under
# services/*/tests was shipping into the production images - measured at 83 test
# files, 556 KB of the 1744 KB /app/services tree (32%). Nothing imports them at
# runtime and the build uses --no-install-project, so they are pure payload.
**/tests
**/docs
